{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQ9jMyL8BEGdKDRFEsR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `watch::Receiver::mark_unchanged`. It's the opposite of the existing `mark_changed`: it treats the channel's current value as already seen. After calling it, `has_changed()` returns `false` and `changed()` waits for the next `send`. The new test and the existing watch tests pass, and so do the `sync::watch` doc tests.\n\n- **Implementation** (`tokio/src/sync/watch.rs`, right after `mark_changed`): it reads the channel's current version and stores it as the receiver's own. This works the same as `borrow_and_update()` but doesn't lock the value, so it can't block the sender.\n- **Test** (`rx_mark_unchanged` in `tokio/tests/sync_watch.rs`): it checks that the method clears a change made by `mark_changed()` and one made by a real `send`. It also checks that `changed()` waits afterwards, and that the value still reads correctly.\n\nI haven't committed anything; say if you want a commit or PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":842,"cache_read_input_tokens":34735,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":842,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a33209dd-af54-450e-bd63-636450ce4c4d","uuid":"589cced7-4443-491f-a76f-b98338657ce9","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:18:55.681Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQ9j9KMgkmKp6CrUyWh"}
